  "script": "My gym only accepted cancellations in person between ten and two on weekdays. I worked across town during exactly those hours, which apparently made me a lifelong athlete. Emails got the same copied policy. Then I noticed the gym offered free membership consultations until eight at night. So I booked the last sales tour on Thursday, arrived with my cancellation letter, and listened politely through the pitch. When the salesperson asked what goal brought me in, I slid the letter across the desk and said, \u201cEnding monthly cardio.\u201d He called the manager, who insisted cancellations were handled by the daytime office. I pointed to the appointment confirmation promising help with any membership question. That sentence did more exercise than I had all month. They processed the cancellation before the tour ended and printed my confirmation. The next week, the website quietly added an online cancellation form. Apparently the easiest retention strategy had been hiding the exit.",
